G1204.b:
⟪δεῦρο⟫ adv.,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨לֵךְ⁩, ⁨לֵכָה⁩ ;]
⟪1.⟫ of place;
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪hither⟫, with verbs of motion;
⟪(b)⟫ (in cl. chiefly poët.) as an imperat., ⟪here! come!⟫: ⟦Matthew 19:21|Mt 19:21⟧, ⟦Mark 10:21|Mk 10:21⟧, ⟦Luke 18:22|Lk 18:22⟧, ⟦John 11:43|Jo 11:43⟧, ⟦Acts 7:3|Ac 7:3⟧ (LXX), ⟦Acts 7:34|34⟧ (LXX), ⟦Revelation 17:1|Re 17:1⟧ ⟦Revelation 21:9|21:9⟧.
⟪2.⟫ Of time, ⟪hitherto, now⟫: ⟦Revelation 1:13|Re 1:13⟧.†

G1216.b:
⟪Δημήτριος⟫, -ου, ὁ ⟪Demetrius⟫;
⟪1.⟫ a silversmith, ⟦Acts 19:24|Ac 19:24⟧, ⟦Acts 19:38|38⟧.
⟪2.⟫ A Christian disciple, ⟦3 John 1:12|III Jo 12⟧.†

G1219.b:
** ⟪δημόσιος⟫, -α, -ον
(< δῆμος), [in LXX: II Mac 6:10, III Mac 2:27 4:7 * ;] ⟪belonging to the people, public⟫: ⟦Acts 5:18|Ac 5:18⟧; dat. fem. used adverbially (cl.);
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪at the public expense, by public consent⟫;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪publicly⟫: ⟦Acts 16:37|Ac 16:37⟧ ⟦Acts 18:28|18:28⟧ ⟦Acts 20:20|20:20⟧.†

G1221.b:
⟪δή-ποτε⟫ indef. adv. (also written δή ποτε), with generalizing force;
⟪1.⟫ absol., ⟪sometime⟫.
⟪2.⟫ With adv. or relat., ⟪-soever⟫: ᾦ δ., ⟦John 5:4|Jo 5:4⟧ (L, οἱῳδηποτοῦν).†

G1223.b:
⟪διά⟫ (before a vowel δ’, exc. ⟦Romans 8:10|Ro 8:10⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 5:7|II Co 5:7⟧, and in pr. names; Tdf., Pr., 94), prep. c. gen., acc, as in cl.;
⟪1.⟫ c. gen., ⟪through⟫;
	⟪(i)⟫ of Place, after verbs of motion or action: ⟦Matthew 2:12|Mt 2:12⟧ ⟦Matthew 12:43|12:43⟧, ⟦Mark 2:23|Mk 2:23⟧, ⟦Luke 4:30|Lk 4:30⟧, ⟦John 4:4|Jo 4:4⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 11:33|II Co 11:33⟧, al.; σώζεσθαι (διας-) δ. πυρός, ὕδατος, ⟦1 Corinthians 3:15|I Co 3:15⟧, ⟦1 Peter 3:20|I Pe 3:20⟧; βλέπειν δ. ἐσόπτρου, ⟦1 Corinthians 13:12|I Co 13:12⟧; metaph., of a state or condition: ⟦Romans 14:20|Ro 14:20⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 2:4|II Co 2:4⟧ ⟦2 Corinthians 5:7|5:7⟧, 10; δ. γράμματος, ἀκροβυστίας (Lft., Notes, 263, 279), ⟦Romans 2:27|Ro 2:27⟧ ⟦Romans 4:11|4:11⟧; δι’ ὑπομενῆς, ⟦Romans 8:25|Ro 8:25⟧.
	⟪(ii)⟫ Of Time;
		⟪(a)⟫ during which: ⟦Matthew 26:61|Mt 26:61⟧, ⟦Mark 14:58|Mk 14:58⟧, ⟦Luke 5:5|Lk 5:5⟧; δ. παντὸς τοῦ ζῆν, ⟦Hebrews 2:15|He 2:15⟧; δ. παντός (διαπαντός in ⟦Mark 5:5|Mk 5:5⟧, ⟦Luke 24:53|Lk 24:53⟧), ⟪always, continually⟫, ⟦Matthew 18:10|Mt 18:10⟧, ⟦Acts 2:25|Ac 2:25⟧ (LXX) ⟦Acts 10:1|10:2⟧ ⟦Acts 24:16|24:16⟧, ⟦Romans 11:10|Ro 11:10⟧ (LXX), ⟦2 Thessalonians 3:16|II Th 3:16⟧, ⟦Hebrews 9:6|He 9:6⟧ ⟦Hebrews 13:15|13:15⟧.
		⟪(b)⟫ within which: ⟦Acts 1:3|Ac 1:3⟧; δ. νυκτός, ⟦Acts 5:19|Ac 5:19⟧ ⟦Acts 16:9|16:9⟧ ⟦Acts 17:10|17:10⟧ ⟦Acts 23:31|23:31⟧;
		⟪(c)⟫ after which (Field, Notes, 20; Abbott, JG, 255 f.): ⟦Mark 2:1|Mk 2:1⟧, ⟦Acts 24:17|Ac 24:17⟧, ⟦Galatians 2:1|Ga 2:1⟧.
	⟪(iii)⟫ Of the Means or Instrument;
		⟪(1)⟫ of the efficient cause (regarded also as the instrument): of God, ⟦Romans 11:36|Ro 11:36⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:9|I Co 1:9⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:7|Ga 4:7⟧, ⟦Hebrews 2:10|He 2:10⟧ ⟦Hebrews 7:21|7:21⟧; of Christ, ⟦Romans 1:8|Ro 1:8⟧ ⟦Romans 5:1|5:1⟧, ⟦Romans 5:17|17⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:21|I Co 15:21⟧, ⟦1 Peter 4:11|I Pe 4:11⟧, al.; δ. τ. ὑμῶν δεήσεως, ⟦Romans 1:12|Ro 1:12⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 1:4|II Co 1:4⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:23|Ga 4:23⟧, al.;
		⟪(2)⟫ of the agent, instrument or means;
			⟪(a)⟫ c. gen. pers., ⟦Matthew 11:2|Mt 11:2⟧, ⟦Luke 1:70|Lk 1:70⟧, ⟦John 1:17|Jo 1:17⟧, ⟦Acts 1:16|Ac 1:16⟧, ⟦Romans 2:16|Ro 2:16⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:21|I Co 1:21⟧, ⟦Ephesians 1:5|Eph 1:5⟧, ⟦Hebrews 2:14|He 2:14⟧, ⟦Revelation 1:1|Re 1:1⟧, al.; ὑπὸ τ. κυρίου δ. τ. προφήτου (δ. τ. κυρίου, ⟦1 Thessalonians 4:2|I Th 4:2⟧ (M, Th., in l.); Lft., Rev., 121 f.), ⟦Matthew 1:22|Mt 1:22⟧ ⟦Matthew 2:15|2:15⟧, ⟦Romans 1:2|Ro 1:2⟧; δ. ἐπιστολῆς ὡς δ. ἡμῶν (Field, Notes, 202), ⟦2 Thessalonians 2:2|II Th 2:2⟧; δ. Σ. (NTD, 22), ⟦1 Peter 5:12|I Pe 5:12⟧;
			⟪(b)⟫ c. gen. rei (where often the simple dat. is used in cl.; Jannaris, Gr., 375), ⟦John 11:4|Jo 11:4⟧, ⟦Acts 5:12|Ac 5:12⟧; δ. τ. πίστεως, ⟦Romans 3:30|Ro 3:30⟧; δ. λόγου θεοῦ, ⟦1 Peter 1:23|I Pe 1:23⟧; δ. παραβολῆς, ⟦Luke 8:4|Lk 8:4⟧; δουλεύειν δ. τ. ἀγάπης, ⟦Galatians 5:13|Ga 5:13⟧; δ. ἐπαγγελίας, ⟦Galatians 3:18|Ga 3:18⟧.
⟪2.⟫ C. acc.;
	⟪(i)⟫ rarely, as c. gen., ⟪through⟫ (Hom), δ. μέσον Σαμαρίας (ICC, in l.; Bl., §42, 1; Robertson, Gr., 581), ⟦Luke 17:11|Lk 17:11⟧.
	⟪(ii)⟫ ⟪by reason of, because of, for the sake of⟫;
		⟪(a)⟫ c. acc pers. (M, Pr., 105), ⟦Mark 2:27|Mk 2:27⟧, ⟦John 6:57|Jo 6:57⟧ ⟦John 11:42|11:42⟧, ⟦Romans 8:20|Ro 8:20⟧;
		⟪(b)⟫ c. acc. rei, δ. φθόνον, ⟦Matthew 27:18|Mt 27:18⟧, ⟦Mark 15:10|Mk 15:10⟧; δ. φόβον, ⟦John 7:13|Jo 7:13⟧ ⟦John 20:19|20:19⟧; δ. ἀγάπην, ⟦Ephesians 2:4|Eph 2:4⟧; δ. τοῦτο, freq., ⟪for this cause, therefore⟫, ⟦Matthew 6:25|Mt 6:25⟧, ⟦Mark 6:14|Mk 6:14⟧, ⟦Luke 11:49|Lk 11:49⟧, ⟦John 6:65|Jo 6:65⟧, al.; id. seq. ὅτι, ⟦John 5:16|Jo 5:16⟧ ⟦John 10:17|10:17⟧, al.; δ. τί, ⟪why⟫, ⟦Matthew 9:11|Mt 9:11⟧, ⟦Matthew 9:14|14⟧, ⟦Mark 2:18|Mk 2:18⟧, ⟦John 7:45|Jo 7:45⟧, al.; δ. τό, c. inf., ⟦Mark 5:4|Mk 5:4⟧, ⟦Luke 9:7|Lk 9:7⟧, ⟦James 4:2|Ja 4:2⟧.
⟪3.⟫ In composition,
	⟪(1)⟫ ⟪through⟫, as in διαβαίνω;
	⟪(2)⟫ of separation, ⟪asunder⟫, as in διασπάω;
	⟪(3)⟫ of distribution, ⟪abroad⟫, as in διαγγέλλω;
	⟪(4)⟫ of transition, as διαλλάσσω;
	⟪(5)⟫ of "perfective" action (M, Pr., 112 f., 115 f.), as διαφύγω, διακαθαρίζω.

G1224.b:
⟪δια-βαίνω⟫
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨עבר⁩ ;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪to make a stride⟫.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪to step across, cross over⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ trans.: τ. θάλασσαι, ⟦Hebrews 11:29|He 11:29⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ intrans.: seq. εἰς, ⟦Acts 16:9|Ac 16:9⟧; πρός, ⟦Luke 16:26|Lk 16:26⟧.†

G1228.b:
⟪διάβολος⟫, -ον
(< διαβάλλω, q.v.) [in LXX for ⁨שָׂטָן⁩ (as ⟦Job 1:6|Jb 1:6⟧), exc. ⟦Ezra 7:4|Es 7:4⟧ ⟦Ezra 8:1|8:1⟧ (⁨צַר⁩, ⁨צָרַר⁩) ;] ⟪slanderous, accusing falsely⟫. As subst., ὁ, ἡ, δ.;
⟪(a)⟫ generally (of. Es, ll. c.), ⟪a slanderer, false accuser⟫: ⟦1 Timothy 3:6|I Ti 3:6⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 3:7|7⟧ (CGT, in l., but v. infr.) ⟦1 Timothy 3:11|3:11⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 3:3|II Ti 3:3⟧, ⟦Titus 2:3|Tit 2:3⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ as chiefly in LXX, of ⟪Satan, the Accuser, the Devil⟫: ⟦Matthew 4:1|Mt 4:1⟧, ⟦Matthew 4:5|5⟧, ⟦Matthew 4:8|8⟧, ⟦Matthew 4:11|11⟧ ⟦Matthew 13:39|13:39⟧ ⟦Matthew 25:41|25:41⟧, ⟦Luke 4:2|Lk 4:2⟧, ⟦Luke 4:3|3⟧, ⟦Luke 4:6|6⟧, ⟦Luke 4:13|13⟧ ⟦Luke 8:12|8:12⟧, ⟦John 13:2|Jo 13:2⟧, ⟦Acts 10:38|Ac 10:38⟧, ⟦Ephesians 4:27|Eph 4:27⟧ ⟦Ephesians 6:11|6:11⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 3:6|I Ti 3:6⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 3:7|7⟧ (but v. supr.), ⟦2 Timothy 2:26|II Ti 2:26⟧, ⟦Hebrews 2:14|He 2:14⟧, ⟦James 4:7|Ja 4:7⟧, ⟦1 Peter 5:8|I Pe 5:8⟧, ⟦Jude 1:9|Ju 9⟧, ⟦Revelation 2:10|Re 2:10⟧ ⟦Revelation 12:9|12:9⟧, ⟦Revelation 12:12|12⟧ ⟦Revelation 20:2|20:2⟧, ⟦Revelation 20:10|10⟧; εἶναι ἐκ τοῦ δ., ⟦John 8:44|Jo 8:44⟧, ⟦1 John 3:8|I Jo 3:8⟧; τέκνα τοῦ δ., ⟦1 John 3:10|I Jo 3:10⟧; υἱὸς, ⟦Acts 13:10|Ac 13:10⟧; metaph., of Judas, ⟦John 6:70|Jo 6:70⟧ (Cremer, 121; DCG, ii, 605).†

G1235.b:
*† ⟪δια-γρηγορέω⟫, -ῶ
⟪(a)⟫ prop., ⟪to remain awake⟫ (R, mg.);
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to be fully awake⟫ (R, txt.): ⟦Luke 9:32|Lk 9:32⟧.†

G1281.b:
* ⟪δια-πραγματεύομαι⟫, “perfective compound” (v. M, Pr., 118);
⟪1.⟫ ⟪to examine thoroughly⟫ (Plat.).
⟪2.⟫ In late writers (Dion. Hal.), ⟪to gain by trading⟫: ⟦Luke 19:15|Lk 19:15⟧.†

G1296.b:
† ⟪δια-ταγή⟫, -ῆς, ἡ
(< διατάσσω), [in LXX: ⟦Ezra 4:11|II Es 4:11⟧ (⁨פַּרְשֶׁגֶן⁩)* ;] in late writers (Deiss., LAE, 86 ff.) for cl. διάταξις (wh., however, is found in LXX, ⟦Psalms 119:91|Ps 118 (119):91⟧, al.);
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪disposition⟫ (cf. διάταξις for ⁨צְבָא⁩; Sm., ⟦2 Kings 23:4|IV Ki 23:4⟧, ⟦Jeremiah 8:2|Je 8:2⟧ ⟦Jeremiah 19:13|19:13⟧); εἰς διαταγὰς ἀγγέλων, AV,⟪by the disposition of angel⟫s (Alf., in l., Field, Notes, 116; but v. infr.): ⟦Acts 7:53|Ac 7:53⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪ordinance⟫ (C. I. 3465): ⟦Romans 13:2|Ro 13:2⟧, ⟦Acts 7:53|Ac 7:53⟧, R, txt. (and v. mg.; Page and EGT, in l.; but also v. supr.).†
